<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico assigns $500 mln in put options.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico assigns $500 mln in put options.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico said on Thursday it had placed all $500 million in dollar put options that it had offered for the month of August.</p>
<p>The options had an average premium of 23.36 pesos per $1,000, with a maximum of 26.50 pesos and a minimum of 22.05 pesos.</p>
<p>Demand for the put options was $1.978 billion.</p>
<p>The bid-to-offer ratio was 3.96.</p>
<p>The central bank said in a statement there were 18 institutions that placed bids.</p>
<p>Of those, eight were assigned the options.</p>
<p>((--Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 9559))</p>
